attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 31, `eamB` to `yphG`, are carried by 90 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 4% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 95 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 22, `mltF`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **A variable stretch follows**, columns 32 to 43, carried by 82 to 90%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Its genes, `yphF` to `hcaR`, are [[3-phenylpropionate catabolism]] {S2.c32-43, Q}. Then a spine, columns 47 to 70, `suhB` to `der`, carries [[Fe-S cluster assembly]] at columns 49 to 56 {S5, Q}. A branch of 4 shell families runs through columns 71 to 74, [[autotransporter]] {S6.b71, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 97 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.18 against 0.36 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 59, `timP`, is a spine column, at 1.03 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 71 to 79, carried by 44 to 90%, are named 82 to 90% {S6}. The last column is `pdeF`, in 44% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 95% of genes**, 0.23 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.79 against 0.16 bits, and names fewer genes, 75% against 98% {C}.

